+## Two added local reader comparisons
+
+Only MNS-076/077 use this section. Their input is the decoded notes element of
+the supplied authored fixtures/MNS-001.als after the exact edits recorded in
+cases.json. They have no public Open or Save expectation. The stored text is
+standard XML-decoded attribute text; the spaces in the MNS-076 value remain
+U+0020 spaces.
+
+**Conditional premises.** The current target's field and KeyTrack-list reader
+associations with this input form, and the ordinary reader context, are premises
+of these static derivations. **A3** names the integer-field association premise:
+KeyTrack Id is read as an Int field; the note NoteId uses the Int64 reader.
+No separate public invocation has been observed. The **A1** ordinary Set-read
+post-read checks of REQ-015 remain unchanged; they do not gate these read-phase
+refusals or prove a public catch/lifecycle. **A2**, the same-state opening/Save
+assumption for saved comparisons, supplies no saved result for either new case.
+
+**REQ-MIDI-NOTE-STORAGE-002 local supplement (MNS-076 only).** With the base
+notes unchanged except n3 `NoteId=" 7 "`, the conditional local text reader
+refuses that stored value. Compare only `local_reader_outcome=refused`. The
+unchanged integer table below still gives no public reading/saved-state
+expectation for this spelling; this exact local comparison is the only added
+exception. No case is added for `+7` followed by spaces or any other spelling.
+
+The `validate-notes` action and `local_reader_outcome` are project comparison
+labels over domain input. They require no native call, public validation API,
+particular reader entry point, internal architecture or implementation pipeline.
+An independent implementation may validate at any suitable point. Local refusal
+does not establish public whole-Set/clip rejection, displayed errors, loaded
+state, rollback or saved values. MNS-011 and MNS-038 remain outside release scope.
+
+**input_projection convention.** Select the notes element of the named input
+fixture. The projection edits attribute text on every element matched by the
+relative element path; bracket indices are one-based document positions. The
+listed edit records are exact input data, not a required implementation procedure.
+No element, other attribute or outside-carrier content changes. MNS-076 uses
+`KeyTracks/KeyTrack[2]/Notes/MidiNoteEvent[1]`, attribute `NoteId`, value `" 7 "`.
+MNS-077 uses `KeyTracks/KeyTrack`, attribute `Id`, value `"5"`, on both matches.
+Both projected inputs are independent; each starts from the unchanged base.
+No new fixture or full Set is generated.
+
